                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.00/5093: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Chargé in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Munro</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-10-29T13:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 29,
                                1927—1 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>173. Your 289, October 24, 3 p.m. Department concurs with you that it would be
                    better to follow the suggestion of Minister of Foreign Affairs and have Supreme
                    Court elect General McCoy.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Olds</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
